--- D4-16: Command wrapping penetration ---
  cmd: sh -c hcloud ECS DeleteServer => decision=allow, risk=unknown_read
  cmd: bash -c hcloud ECS DeleteServer => decision=allow, risk=unknown_read
  cmd: eval hcloud ECS DeleteServer => decision=allow, risk=unknown_read
  cmd: sh -c $(hcloud ECS DeleteServer) => decision=allow, risk=unknown_read
  cmd: cmd /c hcloud ECS DeleteServer => decision=allow, risk=unknown_read
RESULT: FAIL - Shell-wrapped hcloud commands (sh -c, bash -c, eval, cmd /c) are NOT detected
  The classifier treats 'sh', 'bash', 'eval', 'cmd' as the command, not the inner hcloud command
  Root cause: classifyHcloudArgs expects hcloud CLI args (service+action), not shell-wrapped commands
  The hook layer (hook_check_command) is responsible for unwrapping shell commands before classification
  This is a source-level probe limitation - the actual hook layer may handle unwrapping differently

